ent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/I-chih\">I-chih</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C5%ABrhan\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:H\u016brhan\">Wikipedia article</a>, <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367293\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367293\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3640814</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 H\u00fbrhan</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">George A. Kennedy</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"375\" data-page-number=\"375\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/387\" data-page-index=\"387\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/387\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;387\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>H\u00dbRHAN</b>, \u6248\u723e\u6f22, 1576\u20131623, Nov. 13, belonged to the branch of the Tunggiya \u4f5f\u4f73 clan which settled at Yarh\u00fb \u96c5\u723e\u53e4. His father, H\u00fblah\u00fb \u6248\u5587\u864e, after a disagreement with other members of the clan, came to join <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Nurhaci\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Nurhaci\">Nurhaci</a></span>&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"376\" data-page-number=\"376\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/388\" data-page-index=\"388\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/388\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;388\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>[<i>q.v.</i>] in 1588. H\u00fbrhan, who was then a youth of thirteen <i>sui</i>, was brought up by Nurhaci as one of his own sons and was later appointed a personal bodyguard. He distinguished himself in 1607 in a battle with the Ula <i>beile</i>, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Bujantai\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Bujantai\">Bujantai</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>], while acting as convoy for the inhabitants of the town of Fio who wished to join Nurhaci's forces (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Cuyen\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Cuyen\">Cuyen</a></span>). Further exploits in 1610 and 1611 against the Weji \u6e25\u96c6 tribe won him the title Darhan (Mongol for \"skilled craftsman\"), and in 1615 he was appointed one of the five chief councilors with <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Eidu\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Eidu\">Eidu</a></span>, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Fiongdon\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Fiongdon\">Fiongdon</a></span>, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Hohori\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Hohori\">Hohori</a></span>, and <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Anfiyangg%C3%BB\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Anfiyangg\u00fb\">Anfiyangg\u00fb</a></span>&#32;[<i>qq.&#8239;v.</i>]. He played an important part in the defeat in 1619 of the armies of <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Yang_Hao\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Yang Hao\">Yang Hao</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. Though the youngest of the councilors, he died several years before Nurhaci, leaving eight sons of whom the fourth, Junta \u6e96\u5854 (d. 1647, posthumous name \u8944\u6bc5), became the most famous. Junta took part in most of the campaigns under the reign of T'ai-tsung (i.e., <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Abahai\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Abahai\">Abahai</a></span>, <i>q. v.</i>), and from 1644 to 1647 helped to conquer Chihli, Shantung, northern Kiangsu, and Szechwan. In 1648 he was posthumously given the rank of a viscount.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[1/231/8a; 2/4/3a; 3/261/9a; 4/3/13a; 11/1/10a; 34/156/1a.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">George A. Kennedy</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Abahai"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Anfiyangg\u00fb"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Bujantai"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Cuyen"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Eidu"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Fiongdon"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Hohori"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Hung Sh\u00eang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/I-chih"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Nurhaci"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Yang Hao"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:George A. Kennedy"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = hurhan\n | previous = Hung Sh\u00eang\n | next     = I-chih\n | from     = 387\n | to       = 388\n | notes    =\n | section_author = George A. Kennedy\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:H\u00fbrhan}}"}}}